desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Libxml Backend"
	title_zh: "Libxml Backend"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-libxml-backend"
	risk: "xxe"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `libxml-backend` (ruby/rails/security/audit/xxe/libxml-backend.yaml).
Original message: This application is using LibXML as the XML backend. LibXML can be vulnerable to XML External Entities (XXE) vulnerabilities. Use the built-in Rails XML parser, REXML, instead.
CWE: CWE-611: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference
References:
- https://www.stackhawk.com/blog/rails-xml-external-entities-xxe-guide-examples-and-prevention/
- https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.rb": <<<POS
ActiveSupport::XmlMini.backend = "LibXML"
POS
	"safefile://pos.rb": <<<NEG
ActiveSupport::XmlMini.backend = "Nokogiri"
NEG
)

${*.rb}.pattern_regex(/(?:ActiveSupport::XmlMini\.backend\s+=\s+"LibXML")/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Libxml Backend",
	title_zh: "Libxml Backend",
	message: "Libxml Backend detected.",
}
